isn't clean if the assertion is not true, this doesn't work that way for direct mode and V6.\nI think the pain of having it not work at all currently is more important than figuring out a way to shorten debugging time by a few seconds.\nAgree, @yarikoptic , @mih ?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1485420142,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3NTMzNDc5MQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1180#issuecomment-275334791"},"message":"I think that would be an overreaction. Why not keep `ok_clean_git()` do what it does now, unless it encounters a direct mode repo. In the latter case it could do something less or different (like you suggested). I am increasingly under the impression that direct mode is something that won't be with us for too long. But we should nevertheless have some basic support for it.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1485420253,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3NTMzNTEzOQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1180#issuecomment-275335139"},"message":"Right, but guess taht part won't work for V6 as well","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1485420715,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3NTMzNjU0Mg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1180#issuecomment-275336542"},"message":"This is likely true, but we still have a lot to learn which parts of our logic are invalid for V6. Disabling any errors without having identified the root causes will not do us a favor. For direct mode OTOH I think we have clearly identified the problem (a work tree that is not a work tree).","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1485487913,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3NTU4MTcyMw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1180#issuecomment-275581723"},"message":"Tried to keep current behaviour in PR #1231. (https://github.com/datalad/datalad/pull/1231/commits/2550682cdcfb93427ea39415987d77797368713f)\n\nDidn't manage to do it entirely yet. However, it generally works for direct mode now.\n\nBut I suspect you misunderstood my intention, @mih: I didn't propose to disable any error! Instead the consequence would be to loose the functionality of `ok_clean_git` to specify modifications, that are ignored when determining whether the repo is clean and the more detailed output when `ok_clean_git` fails. But it would still consider the very same things to be (not) clean.","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1486664433,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50OTU2MDYyMjAz"},"status":2}]}